From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 08:57:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 126/225] arm64: dts: sprd: ums512: port thermal sensors and
 cooling maps

Ports the 6.16 thermal bring-up: the cache-efuse nvmem shadow (calibration
cells only - the unused DVFS-bin cells were dropped, nothing references
them on either kernel), ap_thm0/1/2 sensor controllers under the aon bus,
and the thermal-zones with 70C passive / 110C critical trips wired to the
cpufreq cooling devices (CPU0 = little cluster leader, CPU6 = big).

Without this the 7.1 cpufreq driver's cooling-device registration had
nothing to attach to - no throttle trip and no thermal shutdown backstop.

Confirmed on-device: all 12 zones report calibrated temperatures (22-58C
range) and cooling_device0-2 register. Flashed via vendor_boot_a only
(DT-only change).
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/ums512.dtsi | 517 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 517 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/ums512.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/ums512.dtsi
index 47de4fafb..176a8ec1b 100644
